{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From the fire.</b> Everything separated through fire." "<b>This shall be for you most holy.</b> What is this? Which offering do we find, besides the sin-offering and besides the guilt-offering, that is most holy? An elevation-offering is not eaten, and peace-offerings are not most holy — so it speaks of nothing other than the two loaves and the showbread." "<b>And for all their guilt that they restore to Me.</b> This expression applies to a guilt-offering, as it is written: ״האשם המושב לה׳ לכהן״." "<b>Most holy — it is yours.</b> The portion that reaches you from all these matters — it is holy, set apart from the rest of the holy things."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:29.014879983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}